## Soundness invariant 3: the average sentence

Carried in the statement comment of `psl211_row_word_proximity` and in the
statement comment of `psl211_word_proximity_close`. The claim is an average
over the deck description and the cut. It is not a statement at a fixed deck
description: a coalition below the threshold does not read an ideal cut the
same way at every run argument. The refuted proposition is
`coalition_reading_constancy` of
`instances/psl211/psl211_spectral_constancy.v`, an equality of two pushforward
laws of the reading of a named ideal cut at two run arguments, and three
lemmas of that file refute it, each witnessed at `psl211_perdeck_coalition`,
the three seats 0, 1 and 2.

| lemma | which ideal cut | which execution |
|---|---|---|
| `psl211_alldecks_constancy_false` (`:258`) | the group-uniform cut law | the all-decks run |
| `psl211_alldecks_constancy_false_word584` (`:769`) | every cut within `eps` of the 584-letter word law this row's model draws, once `(2^-40 + eps) + (2^-40 + eps) < 1/660` | the all-decks run |
| `psl211_dealt_constancy_false` (`:953`) | the group-uniform cut law | the dealer-dealt run, a different execution |

The third is at a different execution from this row's, and the second is the
refutation at this row's own cut law. Those refutations stay true beside this
row and all three are cited by name in the row's comment.

Word gloss, used in every comment of the two files. A deck description is the
whole run argument, a chirality bit together with a deal. A deal is the block
line, the labelling of the heart codes and the labelling of the club codes, the
three coordinates other than the secret. The secret is the chirality bit.

## Recorded rejections

Both are written with `Fail` in `p6_mutations.v`. The decisive error line of
each was obtained by compiling the same term without `Fail` in the scratchpad,
since `rocq compile` echoes nothing for a `Fail` guard. Each rejection is of
one written term and is no proof that no term exists.

**The tautology probe on the distance lemma.** `var_dist_le2` of
`lib/var_dist_supp.v` proves the distance lemma at two with no fact about the
instance and no fact about the walk, and is rejected at `2^-40`:

```
The term "var_dist_le2 ?P ?Q" has type "is_true (var_dist ?P ?Q <= 2)"
while it is expected to have type
 "is_true (var_dist (psl211_wordP R) (psl211_alldecksP R) <= 2 ^- 40)".
```

The pair places the whole content of `psl211_word_lawE` in
`psl211_word_mixing`. The accepted half is kept as `psl211_word_law_le2`.

**A certificate naming another instance's exact family.** `pgl27_exact_family`
as `ipc_ideal` of a twelve-card certificate:

```
The term "amf_sample pgl27_exact_family R tt" has type
 "SampleAdapter R (OE.oe_execution pgl27_exec.pgl27_observed)"
while it is expected to have type
 "SampleAdapter R (instance_exec psl211_alldecks_params)".
```

The field is rejected at its type, before any distance is looked at.

**A certificate whose ideal is the model it is about.** `ipc_ideal` set to
`amf_sample psl211_word_family R idx`, the certificate's own model:

```
The term "erefl" has type
 "ipc_ideal (psl211_word_proximity_cert R idx) =
  ipc_ideal (psl211_word_proximity_cert R idx)"
while it is expected to have type
 "ipc_ideal (psl211_word_proximity_cert R idx) =
  amf_sample psl211_word_family R idx".
```

The two sides of `ipc_close` would then be one term and the field would hold
at zero, so the number published would bound a distance from the model to
itself. Beside that rejection stand the two accepted checks
`psl211_word_proximity_cert_secretE`, that the certificate's secret and the
secret its witness carries are one term, and
`psl211_word_proximity_cert_secretTE`, that the carrier is `bool` and not a
one-point type. Together with the ceiling pair those close the three vacuity
shapes `audit-stageB-fix1.md` N2 named.

